#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpager; gives you a thumbnail sketch of all your desktops. It is a handy "
"tool to let you see, resize or close windows on any desktop and move windows "
"around within or between desktops."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kpager;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &kpager;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:92 index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot"
msgstr "Ecran"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "More &kpager; features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpager; can show all virtual desktops and the applications within them. It "
"can be used to choose an application or even to move applications within "
"virtual desktops or to others."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Reference"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "The main &kpager; window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the mouse"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &kpager; you can activate applications by clicking them with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &MMB; can be used for dragging applications within &kpager;. "
"Applications can either be moved within a virtual desktop or to another one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clicking with the &RMB; anywhere in &kpager; will open a context menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Context Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The context menu depends on where the &RMB; is clicked: If it is clicked on "
"the empty background of &kpager;, it only has two items: "
"<guimenuitem>Configure KPager</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Quit</"
"guimenuitem>. Otherwise, if clicked on a window, there are also the name and "
"the icon of the application, and <guimenuitem>Minimize</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Maximize</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Sticky/Unsticky</"
"guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>To Desktop</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Close</"
"guimenuitem> are displayed. See below for a detailed description of the menu "
"items."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Maximize"
msgstr "Maximizar"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Maximizes the application window to the whole desktop. This item only "
"appears if right clicked on an application window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Minimize"
msgstr "Minimizar"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Iconifies the application. This item only appears if right clicked on an "
"application window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sticky/Unsticky"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Makes the application sticky or unsticky. This item only appears if right "
"clicked on an application window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Desktop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sends the application window to the chosen virtual desktop, or to all the "
"desktop if choosing <guimenuitem>All Desktops</guimenuitem>. This item only "
"appears if right clicked on an application window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close"
msgstr "Tampar"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Closes the clicked application. This item only appears if right clicked on "
"an application window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:189
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Configure Pager"
msgid "Configure KPager"
msgstr "Configurar Pager"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Opens</action> the <link linkend=\"kpager-settings\">settings "
"dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quit"
msgstr "Quitar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Quits</action> &kpager;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Settings Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here is a screenshot of the settings dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the settings dialog you will find four check boxes and two groups of "
"radio buttons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable Window Dragging"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this box is checked, you can drag windows inside of &kpager; with the "
"&MMB;. Windows can be dragged over the desktop or even to another desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this box is checked, the names of the desktops are shown in the main view "
"of &kpager;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Number"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this box is checked, the numbers of the desktops are shown in the main "
"view of &kpager;. If it is checked together with the <guilabel>Show Name</"
"guilabel> box, the name is displayed with ordinals, &eg; <guilabel>1. "
"Desktop</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this box is checked, the applications on the desktops are shown in "
"&kpager; as small views. Otherwise, &kpager; will remain empty, just for "
"choosing the virtual desktops."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "Type of Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group of radio buttons sets the kind of view for the application window "
"views. <guilabel>Plain</guilabel> will show just empty rectangles with the "
"proportions of the application window, <guilabel>Icon</guilabel> will show "
"them with their standard icon and <guilabel>Pixmap</guilabel> with a small "
"view of the contents of the application window. Note that using the pixmap "
"mode is only recommended for very fast machines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "Layout"
msgstr "Presentacion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this group the layout of the &kpager; main view can be set. "
"<guilabel>Classical</guilabel> will show &kpager; in a 2xN grid like pager "
"applications in some other window managers, <guilabel>Horizontal</guilabel> "
"will show the virtual desktops in a horizontal view and <guilabel>Vertical</"
"guilabel> in a vertical row, which may perfectly fit on the side of the "
"desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions and Answers"
msgstr "Questions e responsas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why could I need &kpager;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpager; can be used as an alternative to the pager applet in the panel. It "
"has the advantage of being resizeable and within this able to show icon or "
"pixmap views of the running applications, move the windows across desktops "
"and run outside of the panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I change the behavior of &kpager;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking the <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> mouse button anywhere within "
"&kpager; lets you chose <guilabel>Configure</guilabel> from the context menu "
"for displaying the <link linkend=\"kpager-settings\">settings dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid "Windows are transparent by default, how do I turn this off?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Currently, you cannot turn that option off within the config dialog, but you "
"can do it manually like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open the file <filename>$KDEHOME/share/config/kpagerrc</filename> with any "
"text editor like &kwrite; or <application>vi</application>. If you have no "
"rights to write that file, you may need to do it as root or contact your "
"system administrator. In this file you will have to add a new key with the "
"name <userinput>windowTransparentMode</userinput> with a number as value. "
"Values are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "0 - No transparent windows at all."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "1 - Only maximized windows are transparent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid "2 - All windows are transparent (default)."
msgstr ""

